.\" Linux Doctor man page
.TH LINUX-DOCTOR 1 "2026-10-10" "linux-doctor 0.7.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-doctor \- read-only health checks for your Linux system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-doctor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Linux Doctor
runs read-only health checks on your Linux system, finds real problems,
explains what went wrong, and tells you exactly how to fix them.
.PP
It never modifies anything on the system. All checks are idempotent
and safe to run repeatedly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-check " " \fIid\fR
Run only the given check(s), comma-separated or repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-list
List the available checks without running them.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-list
List checks as JSON with metadata (id, title, category, appliesTo).
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print findings as JSON (machine-readable, schema version 1).
.TP
.BR \-\-plain
Print plain, tab-separated text (no colors/emoji; grep-friendly).
.TP
.BR \-\-summary
Print a one-liner with score, severity counts, and score delta vs the
previous run (for cron/scripts).
.TP
.BR \-\-todo
Print a numbered, copy-pasteable list of the fix steps, in priority order.
.TP
.BR \-\-fix
Dry run: show safe-fix commands for the findings found (from built-in catalog).
.TP
.BR \-\-fix " " \-\-yes
Execute the [apply] safe-fix commands ([manual] never runs).
.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Browse findings in an interactive terminal UI (needs a TTY).
.TP
.BR \-\-notify
Desktop notification via notify-send when new issues appear.
.TP
.BR \-\-self\-test
Explain the environment: distro, profile, tools present, and which checks
will run (and why others will not).
.TP
.BR \-\-web
Open the visual dashboard in your browser at 127.0.0.1:43901.
.TP
.BR \-\-ai
Add an AI summary in plain English (requires LLM_API_KEY).
.TP
.BR \-\-html " " \fIpath\fR
Save a standalone HTML report to the given path.
.TP
.BR \-\-md " " \fIpath\fR
Save a share-ready Markdown report to the given path. IP addresses, home
directory names, and UIDs are redacted, so the file is safe to paste in
public forums or issues.
.TP
.BR \-\-install\-timer
Install a user-level systemd timer (no sudo) under
~/.config/systemd/user/ and enable it: Linux Doctor runs shortly after
boot, then daily, with \-\-notify attached \- you only hear about your
machine when something NEW appears.
.TP
.BR \-\-uninstall\-timer
Remove and disable the user timer installed by \-\-install\-timer.
Idempotent.
.TP
.BR \-\-compare " " \fIfile\fR
Diff a previous JSON report against the current run.
.TP
.BR \-\-push " " \fIurl\fR
Post the report to a fleet server (FLEET_API_KEY optional).
.TP
.BR \-\-severity " " \fIlevel\fR
Show only findings at this severity (high, medium, info).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore " " \fItext\fR
Hide findings whose title contains the given text.
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-code " " \fIcode\fR
Hide findings by stable code (e.g. services/failed).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-add " " \fIvalue\fR
Persistently ignore a code or title fragment (saved to config).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-remove " " \fIvalue\fR
Remove a previously ignored code or title fragment.
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-list
Show configured ignore patterns and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-history\-clear
Clear stored run history.
.TP
.BR \-\-init
Guided first-run setup: environment summary, starter config, daily timer,
and a notification test. Prints copy-paste steps without a TTY.
.TP
.BR \-\-init\-config
Create a starter config file at ~/.config/linux-doctor/config.json.
.TP
.BR \-\-support
Write a privacy-scrubbed support bundle (JSON) for bug reports.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile
Show per-check durations in the output.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-history
Do not read or write run history for this run.
.TP
.BR \-\-thresholds\-json
Print current thresholds + defaults as JSON (for desktop app).
.TP
.BR \-\-thresholds\-set " " \fIjson\fR
Merge known thresholds from a JSON payload into the config.
.TP
.BR \-\-history\-json
Print run history as JSON (used by the desktop app).
.TP
.BR \-\-license
Show Pro add-on status and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-alert " " \fIurl\fR
POST an alert webhook when the machine degrades [Pro].
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon
Run continuously, re-checking every \-\-interval seconds [Pro].
.TP
.BR \-\-heartbeat " " \fIurl\fR
Ping a dead-man's switch after every completed run [Pro].
.TP
.BR \-\-interval " " \fIseconds\fR
Seconds between \-\-daemon runs (default 3600) [Pro].
.TP
.BR \-\-schema
Print the JSON Schema for \-\-json output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help message.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show the version number.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
No high or medium severity findings.
.TP
.B 1
At least one high or medium severity finding exists.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error occurred (bad flags, unknown check, etc.).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/linux-doctor/config.json
Configuration file for ignore patterns and threshold overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.config/linux-doctor/checks/
Directory for user-provided plugin checks.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/linux-doctor/history.json
Report history for trend tracking and new/fixed detection.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B linux-doctor
Run all applicable checks with the default text report.
.TP
.B linux-doctor \-\-json | jq .score
Get just the health score.
.TP
.B linux-doctor \-\-severity high \-\-plain
Show only high-severity findings, grep-friendly.
.TP
.B linux-doctor \-\-check memory,disk
Run only memory and disk checks.
.TP
.B linux-doctor \-\-summary
One-liner for cron: score=72 high=1 medium=3 info=12
.TP
.B linux-doctor \-\-html /tmp/report.html
Save a shareable HTML report.
